== 7.9 Chapter 7 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [In an ecosystem, matter is],
  [recycled repeatedly],
  [lost as heat],
  [created by plants],
  [destroyed by decomposers]
)

#mcq(2, [In an ecosystem, energy is],
  [created by consumers],
  [lost as heat after each transfer],
  [stored for ever],
  [recycled]
)

#mcq(3, [Photosynthesis removes which gas from the atmosphere?],
  [Nitrogen],
  [Methane],
  [Carbon dioxide],
  [Oxygen]
)

#mcq(4, [Carbon is returned to the atmosphere by],
  [nitrogen fixation],
  [photosynthesis],
  [transpiration],
  [respiration, decay and combustion]
)

#mcq(5, [The equation for photosynthesis is],
  [6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6H₂],
  [6O₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆],
  [6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂],
  [C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O]
)

#mcq(6, [Nitrogen gas makes up about what proportion of the atmosphere?],
  [50 %],
  [0.04 %],
  [78 %],
  [21 %]
)

#mcq(7, [Nitrogen fixation is the conversion of],
  [ammonia to nitrite],
  [nitrogen gas to ammonia and then nitrate],
  [protein to ammonia],
  [nitrate to nitrogen gas]
)

#mcq(8, [*Rhizobium* carries out nitrogen fixation in],
  [the soil solution],
  [animal guts],
  [the leaves of grasses],
  [root nodules of legumes]
)

#mcq(9, [Nitrification is carried out by],
  [legumes],
  [nitrifying bacteria that need oxygen],
  [decomposers],
  [denitrifying bacteria]
)

#mcq(10, [Denitrification returns nitrogen to the air as],
  [nitrate],
  [nitrite],
  [nitrogen gas],
  [ammonia]
)

#mcq(11, [Denitrification is favoured by],
  [waterlogged soil],
  [well-aerated soil],
  [limed soil],
  [dry sandy soil]
)

#mcq(12, [Decomposers release ammonia from dead matter in the process of],
  [fixation],
  [nitrification],
  [denitrification],
  [ammonification]
)

#mcq(13, [Humus is important because it],
  [holds water and mineral ions],
  [fixes nitrogen],
  [repels water],
  [kills bacteria]
)

#mcq(14, [Which condition speeds up decay?],
  [Absence of oxygen],
  [Dryness],
  [Moist warmth with oxygen],
  [Cold]
)

#mcq(15, [Succession that begins on bare rock is],
  [climax succession],
  [regeneration],
  [secondary succession],
  [primary succession]
)

#mcq(16, [The pioneer organisms on bare rock are],
  [shrubs],
  [lichens],
  [grasses],
  [mosses]
)

#mcq(17, [The stable end point of succession is the],
  [pioneer community],
  [climax community],
  [biome],
  [seral stage]
)

#mcq(18, [Secondary succession is faster than primary succession because],
  [there are no lichens],
  [the climate changes],
  [more rain falls],
  [soil and seeds are already present]
)

#mcq(19, [Which biome has the highest rainfall in Nigeria?],
  [Sudan savanna],
  [Montane],
  [Sahel],
  [Tropical rainforest]
)

#mcq(20, [Mangrove trees survive in mud because they have],
  [stilt roots and breathing roots],
  [no roots],
  [deep tap roots],
  [broad leaves]
)

#mcq(21, [Trees with buttress roots are typical of the],
  [Sahel],
  [tropical rainforest],
  [Sudan savanna],
  [montane grassland]
)

#mcq(22, [The Sahel is characterised by],
  [over 2500 mm of rain],
  [montane forest],
  [under 600 mm of rain and annual grasses],
  [permanent swamp]
)

#mcq(23, [The carbon in fossil fuels originally came from],
  [volcanic rock],
  [the soil],
  [the atmosphere directly],
  [living organisms buried millions of years ago]
)

#mcq(24, [Leaves of rainforest trees often have drip tips because],
  [they shed water quickly so algae do not grow on them],
  [they store water],
  [they reduce photosynthesis],
  [they attract insects]
)

#mcq(25, [A climax community in a waterlogged valley is most likely],
  [a grassland],
  [a swamp community],
  [a rainforest],
  [a desert]
)

#mcq(26, [Which gas is released when fossil fuels are burned?],
  [Nitrogen],
  [Carbon dioxide],
  [Oxygen],
  [Helium]
)

#mcq(27, [A legume in a crop rotation adds nitrogen because],
  [its roots absorb nitrogen gas],
  [its root nodules contain *Rhizobium*],
  [it has deep roots],
  [it is a heavy feeder]
)

#mcq(28, [Which process would *reduce* the nitrogen content of a soil?],
  [Growing a legume],
  [Liming acid soil],
  [Adding compost],
  [Denitrification in a waterlogged field]
)

#mcq(29, [Fire is important in the savanna because it],
  [removes dead grass and allows fresh growth],
  [prevents all plant growth],
  [destroys the soil],
  [increases rainfall]
)

#mcq(30, [The initial source of energy for succession is],
  [decomposers],
  [rain],
  [sunlight],
  [the soil]
)

